# Veya Remote MCP — public route (PUBLISHED)
#
# The veya site is served by the **aegis Caddy** container (`aegis-caddy`), site
# block `:8093` for veya.aiinote.com. Its Caddyfile lives at
#   /data/soffy/projects/aegis/Caddyfile
# and is bind-mounted into the container, so it is edited by the operator
# (no root) and reloaded with:
#   docker exec aegis-caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile
#
# Applied idempotently by:  deploy/apply_remote_mcp_caddy.sh
#
# Reachability: `aegis-caddy` is containerized, so it reaches the host through
# the docker bridge gateway. The Remote MCP service itself stays loopback-only
# (127.0.0.1:8790); a socat relay exposes it on the bridge only:
#   veya-remote-mcp-bridge.service: 172.18.0.1:8792 -> 127.0.0.1:8790
#
# Inserted BEFORE the veya site's existing `handle /mcp/*` (which still points
# at the Veya backend 172.18.0.1:8767 and is unchanged):
#
#     handle /mcp {
#         reverse_proxy 172.18.0.1:8792
#     }
#     handle /mcp/health {
#         reverse_proxy 172.18.0.1:8792
#     }
#
# Verify:
#   curl -s https://veya.aiinote.com/mcp/health
#   # -> {"status":"ok", ..., "auth_configured":true, "tools":17}
